-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/a289436b-ea74-4eed-afed-7ceb76657e4b
-- title:
--   Incomplete phase observations arise from a restart or observation abort
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$, let $[n]=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$, and let $o_1,o_2$ be arbitrary Boolean independence-query functions on subsets of $[n]$. Paired states are subsets of $[n]\times\{0,1\}$. Let $\mathcal T$ be the class with one label per pair. A defect $(u,v)$ has empty pair $u$, full pair $v$, and one label in every other pair, with $u\ne v$. Put $d(x)=n-\operatorname{pairedRank}(r,o_1,o_2,x)$ using the program’s rank scans and truncated natural subtraction. If $T(A)$ selects label zero on $A\subseteq[n]$ and label one elsewhere, define for $q\in\mathbb Q$
--   $$C(q)=\sum_{A\subseteq[n]}q^{d(T(A))},\qquad \nu_q(x)=\begin{cases}q^{d(x)}/C(q)&x\in\mathcal T,\\0&x\notin\mathcal T.\end{cases}$$Let $p=(\varepsilon,\delta)\in\mathbb Q^2$ satisfy $0<\varepsilon,\delta<1$. Write $s=\operatorname{setup}(n,p)$ for the prescribed schedule, with factor $\rho$, phase count $L$, return cap $R$, returns per stage $\tau$, and local tolerance $\eta$. Let $m=\operatorname{blockLength}(n,r,p)$ be its finite tape budget. For a finite Boolean list $b$, let $t_b$ be its bits followed by zeros. Write $Y(t)$ for the single-run output on tape $t$ and $\mathbb P_m(E)=2^{-m}|\{b:|b|=m,\ E(t_b)\}|$.Put $C_a=C(\rho^a)$ and let $D_{a,uv}$ be the sum of $(\rho^a)^{d(x)}$ over defect $(u,v)$ states. A phase cursor is good at level $j$ when its stored multiplier at every level $a\le j$ lies between $C_a/(4D_{a,uv})$ and $4C_a/D_{a,uv}$, and its current multipliers satisfy those bounds at level $j$. A phase-$a$ certificate supplies the actually reached cursor and a successful next cursor, goodness at $a$ and also at $a+1$ if $a+1<L$, and a product update by a rational ratio $z$ satisfying
--   $$\frac{1-\eta}{1+\eta}\le\frac{z}{C_{a+1}/C_a}\le\frac{1+\eta}{1-\eta}.$$
--
--   Assume $n>0$, fix a tape $u$, and let $j<L$. Suppose every phase $a<j$ is certified. Completed observation at phase $j$ means that the phase history, restart, and observation procedures successfully produce data, the reached cursor is good at $j$, and the scheduled observation count is positive. If this completion predicate fails, there is an actually reached cursor $v$ at phase $j$ such that
--   $$\operatorname{restart}(u,v,j)=\operatorname{none}\quad\text{or}\quad\exists z:\ \operatorname{restart}(u,v,j)=\operatorname{some}(z),\ \operatorname{observe}(u,\rho^j,v.\mathrm{weights},z)=\operatorname{none}.$$
--   Here restart uses the reached tables and tape position, and observation uses the current multipliers.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/SuccessfulPrefixAbortBound.lean#L43-L77

